          "sourceRegion": "Question 21, perspective tower diagram below the stem on the left",
          "description": "Heavy vertical tower OT, with h to its left. Pale grey ground triangle OAC; A upper-right, C lower-right and B on AC. Solid OA, OB, OC and AC; dashed TA, TB and TC. Elevation arcs at A, B and C join each sight line to its ground segment toward O. Point labels and separate North and East arrows follow the source. No right-angle square.",
          "mathematics": "OT is vertical; OA and OC represent perpendicular north and east ground directions in perspective. A, B and C are collinear with B between A and C. Angles OAT, OBT and OCT are labelled 26°, 28° and 30°. Projected angles and distances are not measurements. O is a named tower foot, not a Cartesian origin.",
